    description: "**Defect.** `limits.not_captured` is a hardcoded universal constant, not a per-repo analysis result.\n\n**Evidence.** The not_captured list is sourced from a static module-level constant (limits.py:20 KNOWN_LIMITATIONS, comment \"apply universally\"), so every behavior map emits the identical six generic disclosure strings (dynamic imports, eval, runtime codegen, monkey-patching, complex decorators, metaprogramming) regardless of the repository analyzed. Spec §948 frames limits as documenting what the analysis did not capture, and §756 cache-correctness implies repo-specific observed content; §955 arguably permits a generic list (borderline/weak).\n\n**Contract.** A per-repo signal would be expected per the spec framing, or the field should be documented as a static constant.\n\n**Consequence.** The field carries no per-repo information; a consumer reading not_captured to learn what this specific analysis missed, or to explain diffs not covered by captured fields, draws repo-specific conclusions from a constant."  # 7e81
    fields: {}  # 7e81
- op: discuss  # e1f0
